                        </origin>
                        <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_830">Colwich,
                                Staffordshire. Parish church</orgName>
                            <p><q>Dedicacio ecclesie de
                                        <supplied>col</supplied>wy<supplied>ch</supplied></q> added
                                to calendar at 29 May. At 4 October, <q><persName role="dnr"
                                        key="person_3959">Thome Parker</persName> dator huius
                                    missalis ...</q>. On fol. 154 <q>Orate pro anima domini Jacobi
                                    Walkeden.</q></p> Winefred added in calendar at fol. 289v:
                                <q>sancte Wynefride virginis et Martinis ix lc require in fine
                                libri</q>, but the manuscript is now imperfect at end. In the
                            calendar I [that is, N. R. Ker] can only read the <q>wy</q> of the place
                            name, <q>Colwych</q> was probably read before the protective webbing was
                            laid over this page.</provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">Bought 5 November 1723 from Archdeacon
                            Battely.</provenance>
                    </history>
